  "country": "NL",
  "description": "Months (1-12) in which fruit and vegetables come from Dutch production. 'harvest' = fresh domestic season (open field or unheated greenhouse); 'storage' = Dutch crop sold from storage. Heated-greenhouse production is excluded. The source calendar lists all seasonal months without separating fresh from stored produce; FoodMission split off storage months for typical storage crops (apple, pear, onion, carrot, beetroot, celeriac, white/red cabbage, pumpkin, swede, winter radish), following the Milieu Centraal convention (vollegrond + onverwarmde kas = harvest, bewaarproduct = storage). Items with domestic=false are imported only. Items not listed are not covered by the source (no data), not necessarily imported.",
  "source": "Months transcribed from the Voedingscentrum 'Groente- en fruitkalender' (2023 PDF, compiled from Velt information with input from Bionext and Voedingscentrum), which Milieu Centraal links as its seasonal calendar. The harvest/storage split and the import-only list were added by FoodMission from well-established knowledge of Dutch cultivation and storage. The calendar states no reuse licence.",
